2026-10, by PLN:
  Replaced the truncated kvmd error text in the client with KvmdError
  (status, type, message, endpoint). kvmd
  {ok:false,result:{error,error_msg}} is surfaced intact on tool
  results, with the same secret redaction as before. Network failures
  are PIKVM_UNREACHABLE, timeouts are PIKVM_TIMEOUT, and HTTP 401/403
  are PIKVM_AUTH_FAILED. Ordinary kvmd calls abort at
  PIKVM_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS (default 5000). Idempotent GETs retry up to
  3 times on network errors, timeouts, HTTP 502, and HTTP 503. POST is
  not retried. GET /streamer/snapshot retries HTTP 503 once after
  1500 ms. Sources are the dvaerum and dtrukr commits cited above.

2026-10, by PLN:
  HID POSTs, including /hid/print, are not aborted by
  PIKVM_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS. kvmd replies only after the input is
  applied, and a client abort does not cancel that work.
  PIKVM_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS is clamped to an integer from 1 to 600000.
  Body-read aborts and connection resets become KvmdError and are
  retried for GETs only. Error text also redacts the configured
  password, password: value, and "password":"value". kvmd error type
  and error_msg are capped at 1024 characters. GET retry sleeps 250 ms
  then 500 ms. GET /streamer/snapshot makes at most 4 attempts.

2026-10, by PLN:
  HID POSTs now have a per-call ceiling. /hid/print uses
  5s + 1.5 × (4·min(len,1024) + 2) × perEventSec + 5s, at least 10s.
  perEventSec is the delay value sent to kvmd, otherwise 0.02 when
  slow, otherwise 0. A print above 50s is refused before the call,
  because nginx on PiKVM likely applies a 60s proxy_read_timeout on
  /api/ (not confirmed on hardware). Other HID POSTs use 30s. Expiry
  is PIKVM_HID_STATE_UNKNOWN and is not retried. A
  PIKVM_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS value that is not a string of digits, or
  that is 0, falls back to 5000. Values above 600000 still clamp.
  Literal password redaction applies only when the password is at
  least 4 characters, including on the tool error path.
